.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt DISPLAY-LAPTOP-ONLY 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm display-laptop-only
.Nd use the laptop panel and turn externals off
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl Fl if-needed
.Op Fl Fl quiet
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
turns external RandR outputs off and leaves the internal panel.
Use it after an external display is unplugged, or to leave extend
or mirror.
The glyph is
.Xr bosd 1
.Cm mirror-off .
.Fl Fl quiet
skips the glyph.
.Pp
With no options the panel is forced and the glyph is shown even
when the layout is already the panel alone.
.Fl Fl if-needed
exits without changes when there is nothing to recover: no mirror
or extend state, no external CRTC still programmed, and a screen
size that already matches the panel.
.Pp
The shared RandR helpers are
.Pa @PREFIX@/libexec/bhotkeys/display-randr-common.subr .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 when the layout is applied or when
.Fl Fl if-needed
finds nothing to do.
It exits 1 when
.Xr xrandr 1
fails or no internal output is found.
A bad argument exits 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr xrandr 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
